{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars","id":1113751,"title":"Collecting the shards of Tremere Avatars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-09T08:45:15-07:00","id":1113751,"title":"Collecting the shards of Tremere Avatars?","content":"So can someone give me some ideas about a campaign revolving around finding the Avatar shards of the original mages who became Clan Tremere so that the players can absorb them through Seekings? I figure these Avatar shards hold all sorts of secrets that the world has forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:08:50-07:00","id":1113841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars#post1113751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can someone give me some ideas about a campaign revolving around finding the Avatar shards of the original mages who became Clan Tremere so that the players can absorb them through Seekings? I figure these Avatar shards hold all sorts of secrets that the world has forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Two points. You might want to be specific who you want. Etrius? Gortrix? Tremere? The Council of 7? Any of the Early Embraces? There's alot of potential Ex Mages in early and even more modern clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> And second whether or not the shards can be separate while the Vampire is still running around. IF they can be separate you have some level of interesting potential engagment. IF they they aren't well you're going to have to murder a bunch of low gen Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:32:03-07:00","id":1113851,"title":"","content":"My understanding, at least back during Revised era, was that when a Mage gets embraced, the Avatar considers her to be dead and just moves on to it's next &quot;incarnation&quot;, the same as if she'd been shot in the head by a HITMark or passed peacefully in bed at 300 years of age surrounded by dozens of great-great-[...]grandchildren. This may have changed in M20. <br /> <br /> This presents an odd idea: a Cabal made up entirely of people whose Avatars were at one point those of the first seven Tremere. And does such a grouping worry those Mages who try to keep track of Avatar incarnations? Especially when they decide to go off in search of the Avatar of Tremere himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T14:47:32-07:00","id":1113881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1113851#post1113851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding, at least back during Revised era, was that when a Mage gets embraced, the Avatar considers her to be dead and just moves on to it's next &quot;incarnation&quot;, the same as if she'd been shot in the head by a HITMark or passed peacefully in bed at 300 years of age surrounded by dozens of great-great-[...]grandchildren. This may have changed in M20.<br /> <br /> This presents an odd idea: a Cabal made up entirely of people whose Avatars were at one point those of the first seven Tremere. And does such a grouping worry those Mages who try to keep track of Avatar incarnations? Especially when they decide to go off in search of the Avatar of Tremere himself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was left vague in Revised and you had stuff pointing in both directions. Like with much it depends on what sort of game one wants at the table, which is why its important to decide if you can have Tremere and His Avatar as separate people in game... or Tremere, his avatar and Saulot... wow it gets confusing..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:34:55-07:00","id":1113901,"title":"","content":"Vague? I wouldn't say it's <i>vague</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ST Handbook p. 201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages can be Embraced as any other mortal. Unfortunately <b>the Embrace severs the Mage's Avatar (as normal Death does)</b>, making him a normal vampire<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Contradictory? . While I can't think on any clear example on Revised and beyond right now that contradicts ST Handbook, I would bet this is true. We're talkig of Mage after all.<br /> <br /> Also, you could say that the ritual that transformed the first Tremere into vampires works different than the Embrace.After all, it's not a traditional Embrace.<br /> <br /> Being a Ghoul may shatter the Avatar in Revised, one could say that vampire's avatars aren't killed just because death allows them to detach from their mages. Tremere wanted to keep his magick. Hermetics weren't very aware of the Avatar back then, but, who knows?, ol' Tremere may have known enough to try to forcibly keep the Gift inside their bodies...and perhaps their avtars shattered in the process.<br /> <br /> Albeit I would say that searching for an Avatar would be easier if that Avatar it's complete. Does a shattered avatar retain it's memories?, if that's so, do they retain shattered memories?, can they reincarnate or you will have to search them in the Umbra?. Ascencion states that they can enter in people, but I think the other questions remain unanswered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-09-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:16:48-07:00","id":1113969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1113841#post1113841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Two points. You might want to be specific who you want. Etrius? Gortrix? Tremere? The Council of 7? Any of the Early Embraces? There's alot of potential Ex Mages in early and even more modern clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> And second whether or not the shards can be separate while the Vampire is still running around. IF they can be separate you have some level of interesting potential engagment. IF they they aren't well you're going to have to murder a bunch of low gen Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original members of the House, and since the Tremere's Avatar &quot;died&quot; as he himself put it in Blood Treachery and in other places the Avatars are described as being destroyed, I assume their in pieces somewhere in the Umbra. Realistically, something probably ate them, but maybe the pieces can still be recovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-09-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:09:46-07:00","id":1114031,"title":"","content":"In my Sorcerers Crusade chronicle the Players share a potent Avatar (Twin Souls merit but geared towards 5 chars).<br /> One player took an enemy, an old Tremere sorceress. I decided, that she had the Avatar of this player in life.<br /> <br /> She will try to get \u201cher\u201c Avatar back.<br /> <br /> So I am in favour of your idea.<br /> You can give each player the shattered Avatar merit and force them to start with a low Avatar trait.<br /> <br /> I gave the players Daemon 2 plus unbeknownst to them the Twin Souls merit for free.<br /> <br /> If you give out Avatar 1 and the merit shattered Avatar for free, they will not complain.<br /> Each time they find an Avatar of some old Tremere they divide the rating between themselves and go to a seeking, probably group style. Sharing the Avatar, it makes sense that they share the Seeking as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:27:23-07:00","id":1114346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1113969#post1113969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original members of the House, and since the Tremere's Avatar &quot;died&quot; as he himself put it in Blood Treachery and in other places the Avatars are described as being destroyed, I assume their in pieces somewhere in the Umbra. Realistically, something probably ate them, but maybe the pieces can still be recovered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, while the other books were fairly ambiguous on the point of the Avatar's persistence post-Embrace, Blood Treachery put its foot down squarely on the &quot;Utterly Annihilated&quot; side. Indeed, it went so far with that idea, it made even the presence of vampiric Vitae in a mage's system as being toxic (yet also addictive) to the Avatar, until it slowly destroyed over time.<br /> <br /> I believe I've made my disagreement with this mechanic known in the past, since a destroyed Avatar doesn't lend itself to as many stories as a displaced one. (Not to mention I find Blood Treachery's treatment of mage ghouldom to be overly punitive in general, when the very act of being a blood junkie provides for more than enough pathos). So I prefer to just have the Avatar move on, allowing a vampire to eventually cross paths with it again.<br /> <br /> Still, this doesn't necessarily preclude the idea of specific Avatars coming out of the Embrace worse than others. Especially since the creation of the Tremere vampires was an unusual one. If we assume that Avatars cannot stand the full infusion of Vitae - hence why they don't stick around even though an Embraced mage is &quot;revived&quot; - the Avatars of the Tremere founders could have violently ejected themselves as they performed their grisly rite. So violently, they broke apart upon exiting.<br /> <br /> It would easily justify a character having the Shattered Avatar Merit. I don't think Avatars would appreciate absorbing shards of Avatars other than themselves, though. Maybe if the PCs don't have shards of those Avatars, they could still profit from retrieving them. Either by performing some kind of rite to communicate with the shards (and thus derive memories from them), or by bringing them to mages who share the Avatar, in exchange for knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:09:33-07:00","id":1114454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1114346#post1114346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, while the other books were fairly ambiguous on the point of the Avatar's persistence post-Embrace, Blood Treachery put its foot down squarely on the &quot;Utterly Annihilated&quot; side. Indeed, it went so far with that idea, it made even the presence of vampiric Vitae in a mage's system as being toxic (yet also addictive) to the Avatar, until it slowly destroyed over time.<br /> <br /> I believe I've made my disagreement with this mechanic known in the past, since a destroyed Avatar doesn't lend itself to as many stories as a displaced one. (Not to mention I find Blood Treachery's treatment of mage ghouldom to be overly punitive in general, when the very act of being a blood junkie provides for more than enough pathos). So I prefer to just have the Avatar move on, allowing a vampire to eventually cross paths with it again..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the True Hand v20 book is the final say on Mage ghouls(and is basically &quot;LOL Blood Treachery&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T06:07:39-07:00","id":1114551,"title":"","content":"Yeah. To the extent that: &quot;I wanna be a mage vampire&quot; gets from &quot;how you dare to even suggest that you damn munchkin, the Curse of Caine it's anathema to avatars&quot; to &quot;want to have an awakened avatar in your undead body?, here let's share mine!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you fuel True Magick with vitae. (Actually, it costs a lot of blood) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But well, I agree in that Blood Treachery was far too punishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:16:29-07:00","id":1115937,"title":"","content":"I've got House of Tremere around somewhere, that specifies that they lost the ability to do awakened magic entirely upon their creation and it took decades of experiments to develop thaumaturgy. So yeah, no avatars any more. I'll check exact phrasing - if might be useful in helping with this idea (which will be interesting!) <br /> Apparently the tremere were hermetic generalists, with no specialisation in a particular area of magic apart from teamwork (&quot;hierarchy&quot;) and certamen. It would be fun to bring out these traits in your players, and then have knowledgeable npc's freak out. <br /> Perhaps they should all be hermetics from house tytalus, and in your setting the second massassa war hasn't happened yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:30:15-07:00","id":1116016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1115937#post1115937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently the tremere were hermetic generalists, with no specialisation in a particular area of magic apart from teamwork (&quot;hierarchy&quot;) and certamen.</div> </div> </div> </div>My theory is that if the Tremere were specialists in anything, it would be the arts that would eventually become Mind (I forget the OoH Pillars, and don't have the time to check right now). Given that mortals with prior magical experience are capable of turning that experience into Disciplines, it's likely that Clan Tremere's proficiency with Dominate and Auspex has as much to do with their arcane training as it does the relation to the Tzimisce. I suspect that the first things the Tremere managed to develop were those two Disciplines, as they explored ways to recapture arcane power. It was a little later that they figured out blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:33:01-07:00","id":1116057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1116016#post1116016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given that mortals with prior magical experience are capable of turning that experience into Disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've never heard that before - not that I've heard many crossover rules of the sort full stop. <br /> It seems strange that even if the tremere founders had that, all of their childer would get those as in-clan as well. Makes it seem like all the clans are a bit more caitiff than the impression I got :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:51:06-07:00","id":1116072,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall text in <i>The Red Sign</i> referring to the possibility of shattered remnants of a mage's soul/avatar being rewoven together when they were cured of vampirism, but personally I prefer the idea of the avatar yelling &quot;check please!&quot; at the moment of embrace and departing to continue the cycle of reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:22:02-07:00","id":1116131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113751-collecting-the-shards-of-tremere-avatars?p=1116057#post1116057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I've never heard that before - not that I've heard many crossover rules of the sort full stop.<br /> It seems strange that even if the tremere founders had that, all of their childer would get those as in-clan as well. Makes it seem like all the clans are a bit more caitiff than the impression I got :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the original Sorcerer book, which has general guidelines for how to convert dots in Sorcery Paths into various supernatural powers of other splats. And one of the options is that if a character's prior knowledge fits a Discipline more than a Path of blood magic, you buy that. Presumably, therefore, a Mage works under the same basic idea when transferring to a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T00:31:30-07:00","id":1116284,"title":"","content":"Interesting! I'll have to put that on my reading list. <br /> Does sound like it may have been glossed over as a concept in Revised. Although that may be my experience in the Camarilla taking - everyone always tries to find a way to get some rare discipline or other, so I've heard &quot;I don't care if you were x supernatural creature before your embrace, you're not playing a tremere/ventrue/toreador starting with protean/obtenebration/Thaumaturgy, and we're giving you the Enemy flaw at level 5 with no freebies for it because that background was just a dumb attempt at powergaming but if true would cause you to be hunted by an entire supernatural species&quot; quite a few times. <br /> A lot of time was spent telling people why they couldn't have thaumaturgy in particular, so the idea that all they had to do was find a sorcerer and embrace them, and hey presto you've got a thaumaturgy/protean/obtenebration expert seems anathema to me! But as always, write your own game. <br /> <br /> Oh, and OP - I had a look in house of Tremere, it doesn't specify what happened to their avatars. It does remind me of the two enigmatic entities involved in their corruption though - Root of All and Stars Above. It might be worth bringing those into your metaplot as they most likely influenced goratrix while he searched for Immortality at Ceoris. <br /> Also I've seen it mentioned that Tremere was *not* an especially great mage, possibly was only a linear sorcerer, and was instead very charismatic! Might be worth bringing into it? Have tremere's Avatar be in the &quot;face&quot; of the group? Or even a wild goose chase!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:04:14-07:00","id":1116392,"title":"","content":"I don't buy that Tremere was a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Hermetics have a strict peeking order almost entirely based on mystical acumen. A Sorcerer may be able to do a lot of clever politicking and scheeming from her lowly position, but cannot get up rank from a certain point, and I just can't buy that Hermetics allowed a Sorcerer to be the head of the Major House that was almost ruler of the whole Order without, at least, bieng an Adept. Besides, while Tremere was te youngest of the founders, a lot of time has past.<br /> <br /> I find more easy to believe that the history of Tremere's being a Sorcerer to be a lie to make him look bad among mages, and that the widespread history of Tremere's ineptitude ast magick was merely the fact that he wasn't a Magister Mundi (or, at least, a powerful Magister), like it's to be expected, but a powerful Adept Major or a weak Magister with only one Pillar (likely Corona) at 5, that used it's influence and backstabing tactics to avoid the competition of more powerful mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does sound like it may have been glossed over as a concept in Revised. Although that may be my experience in the Camarilla taking - everyone always tries to find a way to get some rare discipline or other, so I've heard &quot;I don't care if you were x supernatural creature before your embrace, you're not playing a tremere/ventrue/toreador starting with protean/obtenebration/Thaumaturgy, and we're giving you the Enemy flaw at level 5 with no freebies for it because that background was just a dumb attempt at powergaming but if true would cause you to be hunted by an entire supernatural species&quot; quite a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system in Ascencion's Right Hand and in the Tal'mahe'Ra it's there purely for balance reasons. If your player was heavily investing in Paths/Pillars/Watever before the Embrace, you don't want to loose all of that and start from the scratch.<br /> <br /> The system is not there for a powergamer to justify having free Thaumaturgy and unique Disciplines. If the player wants to have these, there are Merits you can buy.<br /> <br /> The Metaplot does imply that an ex mage or sorcerer can invent Blood Magic (which by no means imply it will be among your clan's Disciplines):<br /> *The Tremere are self explanatory<br /> *I vaguely remember Assamites embraced mages in Enoch times to get theirs.<br /> *Tzimisce was rumored to have been an Oracle.<br /> *The Nagaraja were Euthanatos<br /> *Giovanni were, at least, Sorcerors<br /> So, yeah, the background justifies, at least, to be able to research the subject. This doesn't need to be easy.<br /> <br /> I can see a problem with having Thaumaturgy in the Camarilla. Local Tremere ain't going to be amused. If you're the childer of the Prince or other powerful vampire they may not attack you, but they will try to bring you down (or, at least, to offer you a good position inside House Tremere that you won't be able to refuse).<br /> <br /> Enemies among Mages could be appropiate, but this depends on the character's background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-15-2017, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}